          {
            "best_sentence": "Landmark clinical and preclinical studies linking the gut microbiome to immune checkpoint inhibitor response and tumor microenvironment modulationImmune checkpoint inhibitor, NSCLC: Non-small cell lung cancer, RCC: Renal cell carcinoma, PFS/OS: Progression-free survival/overall survival, CTLA-4: cytotoxic T-lymphocyte-associated protein 4, FMT: Fecal microbiota transplantation, IFN: Interferon FMT from defined donors, and precision microbial consortia with ICI efficacy as primary endpoints, stratified by tumor immune phenotype.(3) Geographic diversity in study populations to establish generalizability across non-Western cohorts.(4) Longitudinal rather than single-baseline microbiome profiling to capture dynamic changes during ICI treatment.(5) Multivariate predictive modeling integrating microbiome functional data with tumor genomics, host immune profiling, and germline genetics.",
